# Soma's search, pulled down from home (105+). Bugs from the 135 check on Boss's phone: "dicsord" (two letters
# swapped) didn't find Discord; recent searches never showed when nothing was opened; name searches brought rows of
# unrelated photos. The emulator has no Discord: Chrome and Settings stand in.
# A clean start: no shade or dialog left by an earlier walk.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key BACK
key HOME
# Home settled first: the 138 walk's first pull, straight after the GIF walk, opened nothing.
wait 3000
# Search opened by typing on home. adb's pull doesn't open it on the Fold8 emulator, on 137 or 138 alike (the Mac Pro,
# 2026-10-23), while a finger's does on the phone: the pull is a # The pull itself, on the emulator too (logged, as adb's swipes land unevenly): after a terminal tile has had the
# focus, a pull down still opens search (it did nothing then, the Mac Pro's 138 walks).
key BACK
key HOME
wait 2000
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
shot pull-opens-search
key BACK
key BACK
[phone] step below.
type chorme
wait 1500
expect Chrome
shot typo-finds-chrome
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
# Put away without opening anything: still a recent search.
# Opened empty to see the recent searches: a letter typed, then taken back.
type c
wait 800
key DEL
wait 800
expect Recent searches
expect chorme
shot recent-searches-shown
key BACK
key BACK
type setitngs
wait 2500
expect Settings
# Look: no row of unrelated photos under Settings.
shot typo-finds-settings-no-photo-noise
key BACK
key BACK
[phone] Search "dicsord": Discord comes first, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "andrew" (a contact): the contact with Call/Text, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "beach": his beach and marina photos still show.
[phone] Type a search, put search away without opening anything, pull it down again: the search is under Recent searches.
[phone] Pull search down from the middle of home with a finger: it opens with the keyboard, and stays.
